+        <h3>What survives the control checks?</h3>
+        <p><strong>R3 and R1:</strong> at cutoff d, the negative hi/hi+1/pair signs persist on half-radius loops, while translated controls are positive; all four-state signs are positive (<a href="https://github.com/alanfuller15/Twistronics/pull/2#issuecomment-5844109917">013 review</a>). The baseline signs persist at e (015 and 016). Those e runs did not add half-radius or translated-control loops. R3 also retains the earlier 16 → 32 → 64 point resolution check (<a href="https://github.com/alanfuller15/Twistronics/pull/2#issuecomment-5843439638">007 review</a>).</p>
+        <p><strong>R2 and R4:</strong> 021 compares 32-point baseline loops of half-width 2⁻¹⁶, half-radius loops of half-width 2⁻¹⁷, and baseline-sized controls translated by four baseline half-widths in x. At c, d and e, lo−1/lo/pair are −1 on both centered loops; hi/hi+1/four are +1. Every group on both translated controls is +1. The lowest link singular value is about 0.8249, above the 0.5 discrete-conditioning threshold. Half-radius sampled lower-gap minima are about 0.581 µeV at R2 and 0.905 µeV at R4. These are sampled values, not continuous isolation bounds.</p>
+        <h3>How the lower-band locations were selected</h3>
+        <p>The earlier <a href="https://github.com/alanfuller15/Twistronics/pull/2#issuecomment-5844110028">014 region-box review</a> reports negative lower-band signs at a–d with positive translated controls. Those larger boxes are separate from the local loops in the table. The <a href="https://github.com/alanfuller15/Twistronics/pull/2#issuecomment-5844026482">017 grid</a> located sampled minima at spacing 1/1024. The finer <a href="https://github.com/alanfuller15/Twistronics/pull/2#issuecomment-5844237880">018 grid</a> rejected its fitted points because they lay outside its sampled window. The separately frozen <a href="https://github.com/alanfuller15/Twistronics/pull/2#issuecomment-5844322806">019 extension</a>, at spacing 2⁻¹⁵, gave sampled lower-gap minima of about 2.4 µeV and 4.4 µeV and eligible descriptive fits. Their rounded centers set the 020–021 loops.</p>
+        <p><strong>Fit values carry no resolved minimum-gap information:</strong> fitted minima below their fit residuals are consistent with zero within the descriptive fit residual. They establish neither exact closure nor a gap floor. The <a href="https://github.com/alanfuller15/Twistronics/pull/2#issuecomment-5844184727">014/015 interpretation corrections</a> retract the earlier odd-count inference and exact-zero wording; the numerical evidence is retained.</p>
+        <p class="boundary"><strong>Scope of the evidence.</strong> A loop sign is the sign of the determinant of the ordered product of real overlaps around a closed sampled loop. The 0.5 link threshold is discrete conditioning only. This evidence does not certify a touching, node count, charge, partner correspondence, continuous isolation or infinite-cutoff convergence. It adds no accepted area to the depth-12 coverage result.</p>
