       <details class="secondary-content"><summary>Publication & independent review</summary><div class="review-status" data-disclosed="true"><h3>Results, publication and review are different states.</h3><p><strong>Coverage:</strong> the baseline, batches 001–006 and the depth-11 and depth-12 refinements are published and independently reviewed. Claude gave the depth-12 packet <a href="https://github.com/alanfuller15/Twistronics/pull/2#issuecomment-5842854287">PASS</a>, including 10 freshly recomputed cells. Codex gave batches 002–006 <a href="https://github.com/alanfuller15/Twistronics/pull/2#issuecomment-5841846394">PASS</a> after full replay and 20 physical spot-checks. This supports local isolation and exact area accounting in the fixed finite model.</p><p><strong>Separate evidence:</strong> approximate sampled energies are not area certificates. The graphene animation still awaits its own independent audit. The free-particle wave model is a teaching illustration, and the tracked crossings are historical saved parameter states. None acquires a broader verdict from the coverage review.</p></div></details>
